<section class= "project-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center g-5">

      <!-- Left: Story + Explanation -->
      <div class="col-md-5">
        <p class="description">05 / FEATURE DEVELOPMENT</p>

        <h2>Building the User Account Experience</h2>

        <p>
          I was responsible for developing the user account experience, connecting the frontend interface with backend logic and database data. My work covered authentication and registration, account management, form validation, and dynamically displaying user-specific information across the website.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>01 — Authentication & Registration</h3>
          <p>
             I developed the registration and login experience to support secure user authentication and account access.

The registration and login forms are presented through off-canvas panels triggered from the header profile icon, allowing users to access their accounts without leaving the current page.

Form Validation

Both forms include client-side validation and regular expressions to ensure that user input follows the required format before being submitted. The registration form also includes a password strength indicator to provide immediate feedback while users create their accounts.

Authentication

I implemented JWT-based authentication to manage authenticated sessions and connect the frontend with the backend authentication flow. Once authenticated, the user's login state is reflected throughout the interface.

This established the foundation for personalized account features across the website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>02 — Account Centre</h3>
          <p>
            I developed the Account Centre as a centralized space where users can manage their profile and access account-related information.

The profile page allows users to update their personal information after registration. Optional fields, such as Display Name and Name, can also be completed later from the profile page rather than being required during registration.

Changes are submitted through the frontend and connected to the backend and database, allowing updated information to persist across the application.

The Account Centre also provides access to user-specific information such as order history and purchased lesson data, connecting account management with the site's underlying database structure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>03 — Dynamic User Data</h3>
          <p>
            Beyond creating static account pages, I connected user data to the interface so that content and navigation could respond to the current user's state.

The application detects whether a user is authenticated and dynamically updates the interface accordingly. For example, the header and account navigation change based on login status, while profile information and account-related records are retrieved for the current user.

I also implemented data retrieval through backend routes and SQL queries, connecting database records with the corresponding frontend views.

This required coordinating the frontend interface, authentication state, backend routes, and database data rather than treating each page as an isolated UI.

Development Flow

User Interaction → Frontend → Authentication / API Routes → SQL Database → Dynamic UI

This development work allowed me to move beyond interface design and understand how user-facing experiences are supported by authentication, application logic, and persistent data.

          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

